    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q1-question-1.svg\" alt=\"An arithmetic series has common difference 2 . rd th th The 3 , 6 and 10 terms of the arithmetic series are the respective first three terms of a geometric series. Determine in any order the first term of the arithmetic series and the common ratio of the geometric series. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:580.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q1-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"If the first term is a, the arithmetic term is un = a + 2(n −1). Thus u3 = a + 4, u6 = a + 10, u10 = a + 18, and the three terms in the geometric progression are a + 4, a + 10, a + 18. [B1] Thus (a + 10)2 = (a + 4)(a + 18), [A1] by equating successive ratios (a + 10)/(a + 4) = (a + 18)/(a + 10). Expand both sides and cancel a2, yielding 20a + 100 = 22a + 72 [M1] and a = 14 . [A1] The common ratio is 24/18 = 4/3 , [A1] and the final term is 32, confirming it: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 1 is 6 marks.</p>"
    ],
