    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q2-question-1.svg\" alt=\"An arithmetic series has first term 2 and common difference X . A geometric series has first term 2 and common ratio X . th th The sum of the 11 term of the arithmetic series and the 11 term of the geometric series is 900. Take X &gt; 0. a) Show that X is a solution of the equation 10 ( ) 3 X + 5 X = 449 . b) Show further that\" style=\"--madas-width:580.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q2-question-2.svg\" alt=\"1.8 &lt; X &lt; 1.9 . ( ) 2 c) Use the Newton Raphson approximation method twice, with a starting value of 1.8, to find an approximate value for X , giving the answer correct to 3 decimal places. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:589.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q2-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The general terms are 2 + (n −1)X, 2Xn−1. Putting n = 11, the two eleventh terms are 2 + 10X and 2X10. [B1] [A1] Their sum is 900, giving 2X10 + 10X = 898, or X10 + 5X = 449 . [A1] (b) Let F(x) = x10 + 5x −449. It is continuous and increasing for x &gt; 0, with F(1.8) ≈−82.953 &lt; 0 &lt; F(1.9) ≈173.607. [M1] Thus its unique positive root lies between 1.8 and 1.9. The source omitted the positivity condition, though the prescribed bracket and starting point select the positive root. The equation also has a negative root. [M1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q2-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(c) Since F ′(x) = 10x9 + 5, use xn+1 = xn −F(xn)/(10x9 n + 5). [M1] From x1 = 1.8, [A1] the first substitution is 1.8 −(1.810 + 5(1.8) −449)/(10(1.8)9 + 5). Use the unrounded result for the next substitution: The two steps give x2 = 1.841714560 . . . [A1] and x3 = 1.837954692 . . ., [A1] so the requested estimate is 1.838 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 2 is 11 marks.</p>"
    ],
