      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q5-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"−sin x du/(1 + sin2 x) = −du/(sin x + cosec x). In particular (1 + sin2 x) sin x · −sin2 x cos3 x sin x = − cos3 x 1 + sin2 x . = −1/u The antiderivative extends across intermediate zeros of cos x by differentiation: Thus the integrand is −u′/u. [M1] [A1] Integrating gives −ln |u| + C = ln | sin x/(1 + sin2 x)| + C . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
