    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Differentiate y3 + x2 = axy using the product rule on the right: 3y2 dy dx + 2x = ay + axdy dx (3y2 −ax)dy dx = ay −2x dx = ay −2x dy 3y2 −ax\" style=\"--madas-width:440.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Implicit differentiation gives (3y2 −ax)y′ = ay −2x. [M1] At the horizontal tangent in the first quadrant, x = ay/2; [A1] the curve equation then becomes 2 a a  y3 + 2y = a 2y y y3 + 1 4a2y2 = 1 2a2y2 y3 −1 4a2y2 = 0 1 4y2[4y −a2] = 0 so substitution gives y2(y −a2/4) = 0, [M1] so the rectangle’s height is a2/4. [A1] At the vertical tangent, 3y2 = ax. [A1] Substituting x = 3y2/a [M1] in the curve gives !2 3y2 3y2 ! y3 + = a y a a y3 + 9 a2 y4 = 3y3 2y3 −9 a2 y4 = 0\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q10-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"2a2y3 −9y4 = 0 y3(2a2 −9y) = 0 or y3(9y/a2 −2) = 0, [A1] so y = 2a2/9 [A1] and x = (3/a)(2a2/9)2 = 12a3/81, so the width is x = 4a3/27. [A1] At each positive point, the other coefficient in the derivative equation is nonzero, giving the stated tangent direction: [B1] Hence a2 4a3 a5 = 27 · 288 = 65, 27 = 288, a = 6 . [B1] [A1] 4\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
