    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-z/q11",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q11-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The variables x , y , z and  t are related by the equations 1 1 3 1 3 z = t + 8 t 2 + 1 y = ln ( x + 3 ) = z , 2 3 ( x + 3 ) where x &gt; − and 3 t ≥ 0 . and hence determine the value of dy − 2 Find the value of  z , when t = 4 dt , when y = e . ( 10 )\" style=\"--madas-width:582.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q11-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"At t = 4, √ z = 64 + 16 + 1 . [A1] = 9 The logarithmic equation gives z = 9 ln(x + 3). [M1] Since y = (x + 3)−2, dy/dx = −2/(x + 3)3 [A1]; dz/dx = 9/(x + 3) gives dx/dz = (x + 3)/9 [A1]. Thus (dy/dx)(dx/dz) = −2/[9(x + 3)2] [A1] = −2y/9 . Equivalently x + 3 = ez/9. Consequently y = e−2z/9, [A1] and y = e−2 implies z = 9. [A1] The expression for z(t) is strictly increasing on t ≥0, so this occurs at t = 4. [A1] Indeed (x + 3)2 = e2 gives x + 3 = ±e; only +e has a defined logarithm:\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-z/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Thus x = e −3, z = 9 ln e = 9, and t = 4. Apply dy/dt = (dy/dx)(dx/dz)(dz/dt) [M1] . At that point dt = 3t2 + 4t−1/2 dt = −50e−2 dz = 25 dy 9 , . [A1] 2z 81 The source repeats x in the restriction x ≥0. This calculation uses t ≥0, as required by the square root. At the target value x = e −3 &lt; 0, so the printed extra restriction would exclude it:\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
